diff --git a/src/f1tenth_params/config/stack_params.yaml b/src/f1tenth_params/config/stack_params.yaml
index a5d8556b..d3e6a2ef 100644
--- a/src/f1tenth_params/config/stack_params.yaml
+++ b/src/f1tenth_params/config/stack_params.yaml
@@ -1372,7 +1372,7 @@ corr_wall_turn_k_safety:
   default: 1.50
   description: "Distance safety factor for the wall_turn increment: a turn of dpsi is given k_safety * R_min * dpsi metres. Floor 1.5 -- smoothstep's peak slope, where the S-curve's steepest point sits exactly at 1/R_min with no margin -- and a value below it is raised to 1.5 with an error. AT THE 1.5 FLOOR DELIBERATELY, and the reason is the opposite of what the trigger table below suggests you tune this for. This value does two things at once: it sets the trigger distance (up) AND it divides the per-rebuild distance cap by_dist = d_avail / (k_safety * R_min) (down). The second is what governs whether a turn can finish. Raised to 2.75 to start the bend further out, a live 90 deg wall_turn capped at 42 deg and drove into the wall: by_dist was 0.737 rad on the first rebuild, already under the 0.763 rad horizon cap, so dpsi_this shrank faster than the car rotated, cmd_rot could never advance past its rebuild-1 value and the ratchet pinned psiRef at -0.74 for all eleven rebuilds while yaw crawled to -0.56. At 1.5, with the margin now 0.5, by_dist stays above the horizon cap until d_wall 1.70 m (margin + 1.20 m), so cmd_rot tracks turn_progress + the horizon cap and the ask keeps moving ahead of the car. Trigger distance is the thing to sacrifice here, not angle per rebuild -- the run that failed had committed at 3.13 m with room to spare."
 corr_wall_turn_safety_margin_m:
-  default: 0.5
+  default: 0.7
   description: "Metres of /perception/front_distance (or, after commit, the tracker's d_wall) the wall_turn increment keeps in reserve: d_avail = max(d - margin, 0). Inside the margin, once committed, wall_turn.py drops the distance cap (dpsi_by_dist -> inf, same as an UNKNOWN dFront) rather than freezing it at 0 -- see wall_turn.py's own 'A WALL INSIDE THE MARGIN, COMMITTED' section. FIXED 2026-10-23: before that fix the freeze was live and capped a 90 deg turn at 42-47 deg (by_dist = d_avail / (k_safety * R_min) fell under the horizon cap almost immediately and cmd_rot could never advance again), confirmed on R017/M05_turn_left_wall -- held at 46.6 deg with dFront flat at 0.14 m for 20+ s, then contact. The margin still sets how far from the wall this relief kicks in -- by_dist holds above the horizon cap only while d >= margin + 1.20 m, so every 0.1 m of margin still costs 0.1 m of free-turning distance before the car is relying on the horizon cap instead of the distance one. NOTE this is measured against d_wall, a BUMPER distance, so 0.5 m is 0.5 m from the bodywork, not from the lens."
 corr_wall_turn_commit_lead_m:
   default: 0.4
